# No `kwallet` here: it pulls kde-frameworks/kwallet:6, and remmina reaches
# every graphical flavor through sets/remote -> @extra-desktop. Under gnome,
# xfce or wm the KDE wallet would be compiled and never run. The flag moved to
# variants/flavor/kde/portage/package.use/extras, where it applies to the only
# flavor that has a wallet to talk to. `keyring` stays available as the portable
# alternative, and it is now ON: `keyring` pulls app-crypt/libsecret, which is
# ALREADY in the plan of every graphical flavor through mail-mta/
# proton-mail-bridge (sets/comms). Enabling it costs no new package and gives
# remmina credential storage on gnome, xfce and wm, where the KDE wallet does not
# exist. Under kde both are on; nothing in remmina's REQUIRED_USE opposes them
# (2026-09-11).
